          "id": "bd90fc9bfc7a9431ed6fb0e872b9efff68e997df",
          "message": "fix: omit latency results for unmet recall targets (#6846)\n\n## What\n\nShow **\u26a0\ufe0f Not reached** in the Cohere summary when a recall target is\nmissed, with no parameter or latency numbers in that cell. Unmet targets\nalso produce no latency series for publication or comparison.\n\n## Why\n\nA sweep that stopped at 86% recall still measured its best available\npoint under `@r90`, `@r95`, and `@r99`. The latency tables then\npresented those measurements as though the requested recall had been\nachieved.\n\n## How\n\nOnly reached targets carry a query into latency measurement. Keep the\nachieved recall and unmet-target status in the sweep summary, and render\nthe unmet cell as an alert. This changes reporting and publication;\nprobe settings and the plateau stopping rule are unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cargo test -p benchmarks --bin benchmarks --locked`: 36 passed,\nincluding reached, unmet, and plateau selection cases.\n- Executed the workflow table renderer against mixed reached/unmet\nresults, stale numeric fields on unmet rows, a missing dataset size, and\nempty summaries.\n- Repository commit hooks, including workflow lint, formatting,\nworkspace Clippy, cargo check, and documentation checks.",
