          "id": "1b30ad1b40cfcd754a8c66f91aaba57986f12172",
          "message": "feat(pg_search): deprecate in-index ltree support in favor of GiST bitmap intersection (#6093) (#6877)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #6093\n\n## What\n\nDefines the deprecation window for in-index `ltree` support and\nestablishes the transition path to standard PostgreSQL `ltree` GiST\nindexes via Bitmap Intersection (#6088).\n\n## Why\n\n- **Broader Operator Coverage**: Built-in facet pushdown only supports\n`<@`. An external GiST index covers all `gist_ltree_ops` operators:\n`<@`, `@>`, `~`, `?`, and `@`.\n- **Vanilla PostgreSQL Semantics**: Users retain standard PostgreSQL\n`ltree` indexes and native dump/restore compatibility.\n- **Reduces Code Surface**: Paves the way for removing internal Tantivy\nfacet-to-path encodings, fast-field string decoding, and aggregate\nadapters in a future release.\n\n## How\n\n1. **Benchmark Suite**: Added `benchmarks/ltree_benchmark.sql` comparing\nin-index facet pushdown vs. GiST bitmap intersection across 100k rows\nacross 4 selectivity regimes.\n2. **Deprecation Warning**: Emits a create-time `warning!` during\n`validate_index_config` when an index is created with an `ltree` field.\n3. **Documentation**: Added an `ltree` GiST guide in\n`docs/reference/filtering/external-indexes.mdx` with execution plan\nexamples.\n4. **Tests**: Added integration tests in `tests/tests/ltree.rs` for GiST\n`<@`, `~`, and `@>` operators and updated regression `.out` golden\nfiles.\n5. **Changelog Fragment**: Added\n`docs/project/changelog/unreleased/6093.breaking.mdx`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mahesh Reddy <sunnyyeruva8@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Philippe No\u00ebl <philippemnoel@gmail.com>",
