          "id": "35105117991f0ebde74c77d4e92a36fcd8c3fd59",
          "message": "fix: gate comparison pushdown on collation semantics (#5871)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #5858\n\nSource change is 52 added and 17 removed lines across five files:\nopexpr.rs, aggregate_type.rs, build.rs, pushdown.rs and searchquery.rs.\nThe other 787 lines are the issue_5858 regress test and its expected\noutput. Case 1 from the 09-06 review is fixed in c2205a611; Cases 2 and\n3 reproduce on main at c807edea.\n\n## What\n\nGate comparison pushdown on the operator's input collation. Widened from\nthe original nondeterministic-equality scope per review.\n\n## Why\n\nTantivy compares text by its bytes and `try_build_pushdown_qual` never\nread `OpExpr::inputcollid()`, so two classes answered differently from\nPostgreSQL:\n\n- nondeterministic collation: `=`, `<>`, `IN` are byte exact and drop\nrows PostgreSQL equates\n- collation that is not byte-ordered: `<`, `>`, `<=`, `>=` range in the\nwrong order\n\n## How\n\n`TantivyOperatorExt::collation_operation` maps `=`/`<>` to\n`CollationOperation::Equality` and the four range operators to\n`Ordering`, covering the whole registered set in `opexpr.rs`. The gate\ncalls `collation_semantics::collation_supports()` inside the\n`lookup_operator` arm, where the operator is known.\n\nRemoves `is_nondeterministic_collation` from `catalog.rs`. It duplicated\n`collation_semantics` and failed open: a syscache miss or a null\nattribute both returned false and re-enabled the pushdown.\n\nDeterministic ICU keeps equality and `term_set` pushdown, losing only\nranges, since deterministic equality is byte equality.\n\n## Tests\n\n`issue_5858` now EXPLAINs and asserts rows for all 11 cases, covering\nnondeterministic `=`/`<>`/`IN`, deterministic ICU, `COLLATE \"C\"`, the\ndefault collation, and a non-collatable integer range. Reverted against\nmain it fails four ways: `=` 1 row instead of 2, `<>` 2 instead of 1,\n`IN` 2 instead of 3, `name_icu > 'B'` 3 instead of 2.\n\n337/337 on pg18, no existing golden changed. CI's default collation is\nbyte-ordered, so range pushdown there is unaffected.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Philippe No\u00ebl <philippemnoel@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mithun Chicklore Yogendra <mithun.cy@gmail.com>",
